{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>All labor.</b> He wonders at the fool who did not see good — but is not the essence of all labor so that a person will eat and not die." "<b>And the meaning of \"also the soul is not filled\"</b> is that it is never satisfied, even if it had all the wealth in the world and ate all wheat. <b>And the meaning of \"it returns upon the mouth\"</b> is that it is not filled, because the food immediately descends from it."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "The word תאכל in parentheses appears in the Hebrew text; I rendered it as part of the clause 'and ate all wheat,' though the syntax is compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:54.765734506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}